"<p>SaaSBase manages two distinct types of server environments:</p>\n<h2>1. Remote Servers (SSH2)</h2>\n<p>Remote servers are connected over SSH using public-key cryptography (Ed25519 or RSA).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Keys are generated inside SaaSBase or imported by the user.</li>\n<li>Private keys and passphrases are encrypted at rest using AES-256-CBC.</li>\n<li>SaaSBase executes commands, monitors container metrics, and transfers files through SFTP sessions.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2. Localhost Server (Host Mode)</h2>\n<p>The server where SaaSBase itself is running can be bootstrapped as a managed target node (<em>Localhost</em>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SaaSBase runs inside a Docker container with <code>privileged: true</code> and <code>pid: host</code>.</li>\n<li>It utilizes <code>nsenter</code> to execute maintenance commands and interact with the host system and Docker socket directly without needing an SSH loopback connection.</li>\n</ul>"